    pr_ref:  # 8e39
    description: "router_routes.py ~:145 declares depends_on=[[\"python\",\"javascript\",\"ruby\",\"java\",\"go\",\"csharp\",\"elixir\",\"php\"]]. The 16 concept: router producers' languages are python (fastapi, flask), javascript (nuxt, remix, sveltekit), java (vertx), elixir (phoenix), php (laminas), scala (http4s), kotlin (http4k), haskell (yesod), fsharp (giraffe), clojure (pedestal, ring-compojure), erlang (cowboy), r (plumber). No ruby/go/csharp YAML has concept: router. Effect: Pass.depends_on and prerequisite_absent_clauses are wrong, e.g. a yesod-only repo with the haskell grammar missing is never stamped PREREQUISITE_ABSENT; activation is always_on_unreviewed so the linker still runs. Correct clause: [[\"python\",\"javascript\",\"java\",\"elixir\",\"php\",\"scala\",\"kotlin\",\"haskell\",\"fsharp\",\"clojure\",\"erlang\",\"r\"]]. Same family as INV-tukig (controller_routes). Structural: derive these clauses from the framework YAMLs' language fields rather than hand lists. Confirmed by reading (reviewer + verifier), 2026-10-16 docstring-staleness audit."  # 8e39
    fields:  # 8e39
      statement: "A linker's depends_on clause names exactly the languages whose producers feed it."  # 8e39
      root_cause: "router_routes depends_on is a hand-written list that drifted from the concept: router YAMLs."  # 8e39
